      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHY NOT OLIVIA (1) filled a minor placing last start at Warragul behind Jumbuk Sachin (22.81) in a Grade 5. Has the early speed to land on the pace and can stick on. Comes through a solid form race last start. Good form should continue. TOP KADE (2) stuck on well last time to finish 1.75 lengths back in third (20.15) at this track in a Grade 5 over 350m. Boasts a strong record from this draw with five wins and three minor placings from 12 starts. Expected to be in this for a long way. PAW TREACLE (5) is going well, finishing in the placings twice in a row. Not beaten far last time when a 1.5 lengths third (22.84) in a Grade 5 at Warragul. Expecting sharp improvement this line-up. BANDIT MIA (7) is in the mix following a brief let-up.",
